globalThis.pzCourseExport="# Berberine · course dossier\n\nRevision: Revision 92\ncourse:6087aa3f-a7ae-5db3-9d68-e13c248a1673\ndocumented_course\n2025-01-30 · Switched formulations 2025-03-21 · Generic berberine was recorded January 30; the brand was unspecified then. The March 21 diary records a switch from Thorne to Berbevis and berberine HCl. Later HCl use has an estimated September end. The October depletion names an unspecified formulation.\nDate-window anchor: Recorded course start · 2025-01-30\n\n## Related courses\n\n- Later course · Berberine HCl · 2025-03-26 · Estimated end 2025-09 · The January product was unspecified. The patient places the later HCl course’s end around September 2025.\n  Source · course:4782338b-197d-57d6-9075-647bd45ff8ba | course:6087aa3f-a7ae-5db3-9d68-e13c248a1673\n\n## Baseline before the selected anchor\n\n- 2025-01-03 · Selected activities became possible during better windows · He tolerated some classical music but described worsened burning or fog with much other music. He was frequently bedridden and too weak for consistent notes. He later recalled being able to leave the dark room for the first half of the day after January 8, with PEM and burning still recurring. · winter dark-room state · An individual response could vary by day, intervention or activity. The duration of the improvement is uncertain.\n  Source · baseline_states:BL-12\n\n## Intended targets\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Actions and doses\n\n- 2025-01-30 · Start · 500 mg with dinner\n  Source · 2025-01-30 · start · 500 mg with dinner · consecutive_sequence_aligned_to_dated_posts · reported_use · primary · S1:15447–15460 · [intervention_events:S1-C15447-1]\n- 2025-03-09 · Missed · evening\n  Source · 2025-03-09 · missed · evening · consecutive_sequence_aligned_to_dated_posts · omission_or_hold · primary · S1:27004–27004 · [intervention_events:PZ73-S1-L26990-FL13-0c7e2040]\n- 2025-03-17 · Dose taken · 1 capsule at dinner\n  Source · 2025-03-17 · dose_taken · 1 capsule at dinner · consecutive_sequence_aligned_to_dated_posts · reported_use · primary · S1:28141–28141 · [intervention_events:PZ73-S1-L28128-FL10-0c7e2040]\n\n## Course timing evidence\n\n- 2025-03-21 · effective stop · The unspecified January record gives way to two identified preparations on March 21. The diary names the outgoing product as Thorne. March 23 compares the dose with Thorne; its wording does not establish re-use of that product.\n  Source · diary_fields:S1-L29705-FL9\n- 2025-03-25 · confirmed interruption · The patient reported stopping all supplements during the hospital visit. The pre-hospital course cannot establish use after this point. The individual last dose is undated. The diary dates the hospital hold March 25. The message was sent March 26.\n  Source · archive_messages:S1-M29796\n- 2025-03-25 · interruption report · The patient reported stopping all supplements during the hospital visit. The pre-hospital course cannot establish use after this point. The individual last dose is undated. The diary dates the hospital hold March 25. The message was sent March 26.\n  Source · archive_messages:S1-M29796\n- 2025-11-19 · later phase report · By November 19 the patient reported having stopped berberine about two months earlier. Intervening use and changes of formulation preclude a precise last dose for the January course.\n  Source · archive_messages:S1-M61312\n- 2026-11-20 · stopped by · Confirmed off the regimen by this date. Exact last dose unknown.\n  Source · pz_regimen_snapshot:PZ-STACK-2026-11-20\n\n## Potential effects\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Potential effects reported outside a specific course\n\n- * berberine (0.5g pythosome + 4g HCl): massively helped sudden hunger spikes and glucose crashes · patient retrospective\n  Source · historical_entries:S3:treatment_response:199 | claim:649b6e0b-6312-5520-b2e0-25e187d28bae | entity · Berberine; matching exposure wording, course or administration unestablished (representative record only)\n- Retrospective comparison · Early berberine trial recalled without obvious benefit. · patient report\n  Source · archive_findings:S1-F3199-1 | claim:b6842cec-6642-538b-a341-44c092e0b176 | entity · Reviewed participant role in archive_findings:S1-F3199-1.\n- Taken for months then stopped because of expense and uncertain additional benefit. · patient report\n  Source · archive_findings:S1-F66096-1 | claim:ece31bf0-0d1f-54e5-8ef5-2aea03b19534 | entity · Berberine; matching exposure wording, course or administration unestablished (representative record only)\n\n## Source evidence and qualifications\n\n- [archive_messages:S1-M11354] · reported 2025-01-05T08:07:59+01:00 · We should definitely note down skipped doses · researcher commentary · 2025-01-05T08:07:59+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M11358] · reported 2025-01-05T08:10:07+01:00 · are you taking notes? i can try (i used to) but these days i'm too weak and too often bedridden to be consistent at it · patient account or question · 2025-01-05T08:10:07+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M12902] · reported 2025-01-12T22:17:22+01:00 · update#5: - 'narcoleptic' early sleep last night, 7pm-3.30am - BP=129/104, HR=79 - some hand tingling/coldness - later feet cold - bad burns briefly around breakfast then around lunch. maybe some correlation with KPV? - some gut pain, there was Chinese kale in my meal, maybe that? also, i eat a lot of broccoli and apparently it contains some sulfur - basically despite stopping L-cysteine 3d ago, L-ornithine today, there is no difference in burns, maybe a bit more today - pre-PEM back of head pain onset at 5.30-6 - went to rest in dark room and mostly disappeared. got up and reappeared but didn't appear to be progressing into pem, just a low grade ache in back of head - def a lot hungrier today, ate more than usual too (since you asked) - 2x bm · patient account or question · 2025-01-12T22:17:22+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M15447] · reported 2025-01-31T06:06:55+01:00 · update#17: - how i felt after waking: not rested despite long sleep - PEM: woke w/ minor arm/nape tingling as usual; 4pm onwards leg/arm tingling, shudders from light – didn't succumb to full PEM but was unstable - narcolepsy: 0 - burns: smaller crash 11am; mod. crash at 3pm - tinnitus: - POTS: mod. - stool: 1x, slightly darker - gut pain: 0 - hunger: slight lack of satiation after lunch - activity: usual computer+bed rest - changes: started berberine 500mg with dinner afternoon crash again uncertain whether PEM or PENE, the lines seem to be more blurred these days · patient message · 2025-01-31T06:06:55+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M29796] · reported 2025-03-26T11:55:47+01:00 · update#71: - rating (1-10): 2 - sleep (following day): absolutely terrible, was up more than i was asleep it felt like - PEM: pem in pm after tests and talking to ppl - narcolepsy: - burns/pressures: - tinnitus: - POTS: - stool: 2x in morning one after another - gut pain: - hunger: - activity: - cold/heat: - changes: hospital visit; stopped all supplements · patient message · 2025-03-26T11:55:47+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M61312] · reported 2025-11-19T22:29:07+01:00 · wondering if the berberine is wearing off (stopped like 2mo ago tho...), or if it's just due to being pemy · patient message · 2025-11-19T22:29:07+01:00\n- [baseline_states:BL-12] · 2025-01-03 · through 2025-01-12 · Selected activities became possible during better windows · He tolerated some classical music but described worsened burning or fog with much other music. He was frequently bedridden and too weak for consistent notes. He later recalled being able to leave the dark room for the first half of the day after January 8, with PEM and burning still recurring. · winter dark-room state · An individual response could vary by day, intervention or activity. The duration of the improvement is uncertain.\n- [diary_fields:S1-L26990-FL13] · 2025-03-09 · changes · 1/2 nicotine patch; forgot pea-lut and evening kpv/la/berberine/quercetin · as labelled\n- [diary_fields:S1-L28128-FL10] · 2025-03-17 · changes · accidentally took 2x kpv before lunch; double spm dose (2nd one after lunch when PEM came on); forget clay minerals; only took 1 cap berberine at dinner to make it last longer · as labelled\n- [diary_fields:S1-L29705-FL9] · 2025-03-21 · changes · restart NC; switch from Thorne berberine to 275ng Berbevis + 1g HCL; forgot evening SPM · as labelled\n- [diary_logs:S1-L26990] · 2025-03-09 · reported 2025-03-12T11:05:57+01:00 · update#55: [3d ago] - rating (1-10): 1.5 - sleep (following day): sweated a lot, woke up for urination once (doesn't usually happen); data missing forgot to charge watch - PEM: no PEM at all first half of day; then slow down, take a break, and PEM slowly creeps up to a pretty long and mod/sev crash - narcolepsy: kinda. had sleep pressure so prepped everything for bed then fell asleep. so not as strong as it once was where i would just be knocked out one moment to the next without realizing it - burns: mod-esev first half of day - tinnitus: mild-mod - POTS: mild? - stool: 2x; 1st very normal (think from lentils); 2nd a bit constipated at first then less normal (not exactly fatty but not solid like the first one either, also comes apart, some bubbling to the surface [fermentation?!]) - gut pain: some flares in the afternoon - hunger: more normal but still lower than before. really biggest change is that i don’t wake up hungry and i can go a few hours between dinner and sleep - before i had to eat right before bed time otherwise i’d be hungry and stressed falling asleep. - activity: too much in the first half of day, was fueled by nicotine overdrive; rest of daya in bed - UTI: 0 - cold/heat: usual - changes: 1/2 nicotine patch; forgot pea-lut and evening kpv/la/berberine/quercetin · consecutive_sequence_aligned_to_dated_posts · 2025-03-12T11:05:57+01:00\n- [diary_logs:S1-L28128] · 2025-03-17 · reported 2025-03-18T11:14:50+01:00 · update#63: - rating (1-10): 1.5 - sleep (following day): really long and didn’t wake up much in the dawn - PEM: unstable/pem-y all day, but no real crash - narcolepsy: - burns: some flares - tinnitus: same - POTS: - stool: 1x ar 1pm strangely (forgot evening kpv previous day, might be why), very little came out, bit dark - gut pain: rhs flare after lunch; some bad rhs flare late in the evening - hunger: had a sudden hunger spike close to midnight while coming off the nicotine overdrive, otherwise normal - activity: mostly bed bound, listening to audio book, on phone, very little computer time - cold/heat: feet very cold, especially left one - changes: accidentally took 2x kpv before lunch; double spm dose (2nd one after lunch when PEM came on); forget clay minerals; only took 1 cap berberine at dinner to make it last longer · consecutive_sequence_aligned_to_dated_posts · 2025-03-18T11:14:50+01:00\n- [diary_logs:S1-L29705] · 2025-03-21 · reported 2025-03-25T19:06:26+01:00 · update#67: [4d ago] - rating (1-10): 2 - sleep (following day): woke up again with parched mouth and full bladder but otherwise ok - PEM: crashy from evening but no real crash - narcolepsy: - burns/pressures: still pressure on same spot at left top of head - tinnitus: mild - POTS: - stool: 3x; first normal although a bit light as it semi floated (texture better since starting acacia); rest small dark bits - gut pain: - hunger: normal - activity: maybe slightly too much - cold/heat: warm all day citrulline def working - changes: restart NC; switch from Thorne berberine to 275ng Berbevis + 1g HCL; forgot evening SPM · consecutive_sequence_aligned_to_dated_posts · 2025-03-25T19:06:26+01:00\n- [intervention_events:PZ73-S1-L26990-FL13-0c7e2040] · 2025-03-09 · reported 2025-03-12T11:05:57+01:00 · Berberine · missed · evening · consecutive_sequence_aligned_to_dated_posts · omission_or_hold · primary\n- [intervention_events:PZ73-S1-L28128-FL10-0c7e2040] · 2025-03-17 · reported 2025-03-18T11:14:50+01:00 · Berberine · dose_taken · 1 capsule at dinner · consecutive_sequence_aligned_to_dated_posts · reported_use · primary\n- [intervention_events:S1-C15447-1] · 2025-01-30 · reported 2025-01-31T06:06:55+01:00 · Berberine · start · 500 mg with dinner · consecutive_sequence_aligned_to_dated_posts · reported_use · primary\n- [s1_quote_context:S1-M11358#1] · reported 2025-01-05T08:10:07+01:00 · unverified; see linked parent where identified\n- [source_lines:S3:617] · * 8:\n- [source_lines:S3:618] · * ▶️ Arterosil: increase NO, anticoagulant, anti-plaque, reduces vascular inflammation\n- [source_lines:S3:619] · * ▶️ glutathione 2x250-500mg: since OAT shows impaired synthesis → relief in PEM, since then able to leave dark room for first half of day (previously spent most of the day in bed)\n- [source_lines:S3:620] · * 9: ▶️ L-carnitine 3x4.5g: suspicion of carnitine theft by Candida (as per OAT) → slightly less PEM and higher body temperature, hands/feet not cold anymore\n- [source_lines:S3:621] · * stopped after 1 month → mild improvement probably confirms beta-oxidation issue but it’s not the main problem\n- [treatment_intervals:EARLY-I-S1-C15447-1] · 2025-01-30 · Berberine · 2025-01-30 · hospital_changes_interrupt_observation · Use before the March 25 hospital medication/supplement interruption; exact end unknown. · primary";
